Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:02.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is an existential issue for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.60,0:00:05.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,We could easily stop, but if we stop today, we lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.17,0:00:10.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Functionality, capability, safety, security, they're all at exactly the same place.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.11,0:00:20.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Priority number one.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.00,0:00:22.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's our third pod back together.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.88,0:00:23.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yep.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.36,0:00:28.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,In the last 10 days, you've been uh at the Xi state dinner at the White House.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.52,0:00:33.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you were at the White House uh summit where we did the accord on superintelligence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.22,0:00:37.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and just yesterday, you were there with your parents um when the president, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.68,0:00:41.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,presented you with a National Medal of Science. the only investor at the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.80,0:00:45.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I there You were the only investor at the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.24,0:00:47.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now that now that we reflected on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.64,0:00:48.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.03,0:00:51.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, and tell me being there with your parents yesterday, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.76,0:00:56.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,It struck me five out of the six people on stage were all born outside of the United States.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.84,0:01:00.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um how did that feel?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.16,0:01:05.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh well, first of all, it's a great honor all by itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.14,0:01:09.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and it's a reflection of the the contribution that the company has made.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.04,0:01:14.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and obviously obviously we created we invented a new computing model.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.92,0:01:18.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is probably the most pervasive computing model in the world today.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.24,0:01:20.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's the only computing architecture that's in every cloud.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.58,0:01:21.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's in every computer company.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.80,0:01:24.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's used in every field of science.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.60,0:01:25.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's used by gamers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.74,0:01:29.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's used by creators and builders and it's used by scientists.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.00,0:01:31.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh it powers intelligence.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.60,0:01:32.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.16,0:01:36.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, just if you take a step step back and you look at what what the company has accomplished,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.52,0:01:39.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, we started out building a graphics chip for gamers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.50,0:01:41.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm still proud of that, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.85,0:01:48.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and we've now shipped 1 and 1/2 1.67 billion billion units.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.26,0:01:54.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's how many generations of I mean, I raised generations of scientists and kids and designers, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.36,0:02:03.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so I think the impact that and here we are you know, we're the infrastructure that powers the intelligence of society.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.28,0:02:08.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so it's a it's an incredibly proud moment for me to receive the award on behalf of the company.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.02,0:02:17.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now for my parents you know, I wanted them to go and and I gave them literally you know, 24 hours notice time and they don't travel that much.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.30,0:02:20.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,They don't travel that much and my dad didn't even have a suit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.80,0:02:21.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.52,0:02:23.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so he ran out and bought a suit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.72,0:02:26.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh He looked great.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.61,0:02:27.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,They looked great.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.52,0:02:31.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it was a brand new suit and he showed up and I I didn't realize he was he had a suit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.61,0:02:33.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,I thought he was just going to wear some shirt.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.96,0:02:36.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so he went out and bought a suit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.26,0:02:40.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um my my mom got a new dress you know, and and literally in 24 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.04,0:02:41.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.92,0:02:42.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, I know how it works.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.00,0:02:45.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh my gosh, it's incredible.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.38,0:02:49.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I so we got them on a we chartered a plane for them, got them there.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.48,0:02:54.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so they were so happy to meet the president.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.24,0:03:03.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and President Trump walked my mom because she has a hard time walking and the two of them were were walking off stage and he he held her.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.36,0:03:03.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.56,0:03:09.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And walked it walked her down the stage and they were just incredibly incredibly proud to meet her meet him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.70,0:03:12.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um uh but for them it's their American dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.96,0:03:13.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.54,0:03:16.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,my dad I still remember I was I think I was like 5 years old or something
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.00,0:03:21.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,like that and and uh he had just come back from the United States on a business trip.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.64,0:03:25.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,He was he was working for an air conditioning company and he was living in Taiwan?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.80,0:03:28.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We were at the time we had just moved to Thailand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.16,0:03:28.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thailand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.48,0:03:34.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um Oh no, no, we were just about to move to Thailand and um we were in Taiwan.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.60,0:03:39.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,He had come back and he was he was in the United States working for a company called Carrier.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.80,0:03:43.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're an air conditioning company and uh he was here for training.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.52,0:03:48.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um I of all the places in the world they landed him in New York.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.27,0:03:48.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.64,0:03:54.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so here you can just imagine a kid in the late 20s, I guess mid late 20s.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.28,0:04:00.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh never been outside of Taiwan, goes to United States, New York City of all places.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.76,0:04:03.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And he saw the future of the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.12,0:04:05.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And he came back, you know, mind-blown.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.68,0:04:09.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh all the things that he bought at the airport and brought it back, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.92,0:04:16.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,it was a he bought he he brought chocolate, he brought you know that cheese that you have in a tube back in the old days?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.24,0:04:17.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's kind of like white cheese.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.55,0:04:18.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Strange cheese.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.38,0:04:19.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,It comes in a tube.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.62,0:04:20.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's great.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.36,0:04:26.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh he brought back all kinds of strange things and he said, "This is we should go there someday."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.56,0:04:37.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the first opportunity they had they sent my older brother and I to United States and and um you know, it was it was his dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.24,0:04:40.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't think many people realize that you came to the United States ahead of your parents.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.92,0:04:41.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.24,0:04:42.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.42,0:04:45.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and they joined a few years later.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.18,0:04:52.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,But it just hit me like a ton of bricks that five out of the six people on that stage yesterday were born outside the United States.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.06,0:04:57.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,You and I have talked about the need for you know, with all the other stuff going on,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.18,0:05:02.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,a real strategy and an immigration policy policy that makes certain that we're still
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.98,0:05:05.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,the place that all the great builders in the world want to come build.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.00,0:05:07.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,This this is America's superpowers.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.80,0:05:08.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.20,0:05:16.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um in a lot of ways the intellectual property creation capability of our nation is unlike anything else in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.85,0:05:18.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is we attract the world's best.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.96,0:05:19.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.40,0:05:24.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we are the place where they want to come and build their lives because of the opportunity it provides,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.80,0:05:33.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,the freedom that that she offers, the opportunity that it provides, the spirit of of invention and entrepreneurialism and of the can-do attitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.93,0:05:37.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, in the United States everything is is possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.52,0:05:38.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.20,0:05:40.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We start with of course it's possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.08,0:05:41.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course we could do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.77,0:05:46.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Instead of instead of you know, I I do a lot of travel and of course you can't do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.56,0:05:49.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course you know, In other places. in other in other places.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.33,0:05:50.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we take it for granted.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.00,0:05:51.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,It does.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.40,0:06:00.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the spirit, the the the energy um that comes around with the culture that we've created here, Yeah. um it's just can't be understated.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.90,0:06:11.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And so I think the flow, the inflow of intellectual property into this into this country is unlike anything else the world's ever seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.28,0:06:11.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.76,0:06:12.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we want that.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.67,0:06:19.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want all of the world's great minds to come here, bring their great ideas, you know, make them realize them here, Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.16,0:06:24.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,realize them here and let us, you know, let us let us keep that flywheel going.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.33,0:06:27.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, I really it's a it's a delicate system.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.32,0:06:28.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a delicate balance.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.53,0:06:30.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,I get it's a delicate balance.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.19,0:06:32.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,I get and so we have to do it lawfully.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.10,0:06:33.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have to do it rightfully.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.92,0:06:35.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but we we surely want to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.64,0:06:36.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, for sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.48,0:06:39.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I want to start high level just kind of where we are.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.31,0:06:45.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then I want to dig down a little bit into the safety and regulation and getting this right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.11,0:06:47.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where we are in terms of the compute build out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.53,0:06:53.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then finally we're going to finish up you know, drilling in a little bit to Nvidia's growth and and and and what's going on there.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.84,0:06:56.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,But you've been really good at calling the future, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.69,0:07:02.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Two years ago we were sitting here and you said that the market was dramatically underestimating the amount of compute
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.80,0:07:07.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,build out that was going to be required and was going to happen over the course of the next 5 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.55,0:07:13.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,You You said it's not going to be a trillion, it's going to be 2 trillion at a minimum in terms of cumulative compute build out.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.21,0:07:14.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And of course now we're over that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.96,0:07:18.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,You said before everybody was thinking about it that inference, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.35,0:07:23.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Compute was going to 1 billion X because of inference time reasoning and thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.28,0:07:30.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then last year of course, before we saw Opus 4.6, before we saw Claude code, you said we're entering the age of agents, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.91,0:07:34.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where we're going to unlock a lot of these capabilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.21,0:07:37.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and of course we saw Opus 4.6 and Claude code really took off.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.01,0:07:39.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So where are we now, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.72,0:07:43.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,We We Elon and Sam and And only three things that I said that came true.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.58,0:07:44.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's another 200.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.63,0:07:46.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why don't you just keep on going?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.44,0:07:49.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,That I just let that be the podcast.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.28,0:07:56.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I just So So So our investor day in a couple weeks is on, you know, entering the singularity, this acceleration.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.36,0:08:02.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have Elon and Sam and Demis all say, "Hey, we're in the foothills or entering the singularity."
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.96,0:08:06.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have, you know, model solving Navier-Stokes, as you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.04,0:08:11.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so when you look into your crystal ball, where are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.18,0:08:12.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,And are we inflecting?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.73,0:08:19.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are we accelerating, you know, into a different phase of superintelligence?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.04,0:08:23.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um And so let let's unpack that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.73,0:08:26.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,First First of all,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.24,0:08:33.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's very fairly logical why the amount of compute that we're going to need is a billion times more than where we were just recently,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.52,0:08:34.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,let's say call it last year.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.82,0:08:42.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because thinking and problem solving takes a lot more,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.20,0:08:49.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, inferences than repeating something, regurgitating something that you memorized.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.53,0:08:57.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when you're a ChatGPT, you give it a prompt, most of that most of that knowledge was encoded into the large language model.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.76,0:09:00.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, of course, it hallucinated.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.90,0:09:09.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the next click was it was it was a generative, but it was also grounded or conditioned by ground truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.28,0:09:10.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.76,0:09:14.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,It would have to go out and do a search, do a quick search, comes back with the ground truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.34,0:09:19.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then from that conditioning augment it with his own own what it already learned,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.92,0:09:24.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,pre-training, and it would generate new new whatever the answer is.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.71,0:09:31.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, most of most of the things that we want to really do that are that are interesting requires you to to to reason step by step,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.57,0:09:34.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,to come up with several options, plan,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.21,0:09:35.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,and you might decide,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.50,0:09:43.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,"Let's see how these things all roll out and then based on based on the answers of all of those I reflect on the best answers so far,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.52,0:09:44.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,the best path so far.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.81,0:09:48.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I might choose one or two or three of them, roll them out.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.28,0:09:48.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.60,0:09:50.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, prune the rest of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.11,0:09:51.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then just keep on doing this.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.47,0:09:59.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you know, people we do this that's the reason why why we say um, great strategists love strategic optionality.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.20,0:10:04.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,You don't want to prune things too fast on the one hand, but you you also have to optimize your resources.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.92,0:10:06.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, AI's are doing that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.80,0:10:11.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so so they're they're keeping their strategic optionality, they're rolling things out,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.60,0:10:16.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,they're pruning, um, they're they're reflecting, they're pruning, so on and so forth.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.15,0:10:21.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all of that thinking all of that exploration just takes a lot more compute.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.15,0:10:27.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and not on top of that, because it's able to now do productive things, we're going to use it for more things.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.67,0:10:31.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the compounding of both it uses more compute to do its job,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.49,0:10:35.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it's doing a good job and therefore we're going to we're going to hire it to do more jobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.32,0:10:35.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.00,0:10:36.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.36,0:10:37.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that all compounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.98,0:10:38.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.22,0:10:44.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,at this point I would I would say that the big observation from last year is that that on the
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.72,0:10:48.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,one hand we want the models to get better and better and we we still want the models to get better.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.29,0:10:51.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the scaling laws of models are are going to continue.
